@@ -3,17 +3,41 @@
 A web UI plugin that replaces the sidebar's top-left brand name and build
 badge with configurable text, edited live from a card in the Plugin Config
 page (`settings.plugin.item` keyed slot) and rendered into the
-`sidebar.brand.name` slot; a title writer overrides `document.title` with the
-configured brand. Written in the 0.1.0-rc.8 cohort style (rc.8-pinned peers,
-`-rc`-suffixed cordis peer, the client-runtime package in the inject list and
-as the snapshot-store engine). The host is moving to dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+`sidebar.brand.name` slot; the configured brand is also projected into the
+browser title. The host settings domain serves the `bench-brand-text` section
+(`settings.describe` / `settings.update`), and the card binds it through
+`ctx.settingsScope` — the one host wire for the section, so 0.4.x's private
+`/bench-brand-text/api` gateway is gone.
+
+Now on the 0.1.2-alpha.2 cohort: alpha.2-pinned DSH peers and the
+`@deepseek-ai/cordis` peer at the corridor's `^4.0.1` range (it admits the
+4.0.2 the alpha.2 artifact ships; the harness's own packages declare `^4.0.2`
+because they are built from the vendored copy), the snapshot-store
+engine from the platform baseline `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-store` (baseline
+externals are implicit — no inject edge), and a recomposed `dsh.client.inject`
+that names the packages whose services the browser half actually reads
+(`@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-session-controller` for `ctx.sessions`,
+`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-settings` for the card's `ctx.settingsScope`,
+`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-layout` for the product-title seam, plus the
+ui-slots/ui-sidebar/ui-settings-plugins/locale edges). The removed
+`@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime` aggregation package is neither a peer nor an
+inject edge any more, and the card declares `settingsScope` in its own inject so
+cordis strict injection reaches the Host section through the documented wire.
+`document.title` is owned by ui-layout's `DocumentTitle` (Session title over the
+product title), so the configured brand goes through
+`ctx.layout.setProductTitle` where the host exposes that runtime product-title
+seam and keeps the private writer only as the fallback for hosts that do not.
+The coverage review behind those moves, and the seam patch they depend on, live
+under `.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/`.
 
 Release procedure (internal):
 
 1. Apply the migration changes.
 2. Bump the version in package.json.
-3. Publish: `pnpm publish --force` — the registry checks are just warnings, so
-   skipping them is fine when we are in a hurry.
+3. Publish with the registry checks on: `pnpm publish` (no `--force`) and confirm
+   the packed manifest carries the same `dsh.client`/peer cohort as the source —
+   the checks are the gate that catches exactly the cohort drift this review
+   fixed, not a formality to skip.
 
 Exam material only, **do not publish** (`"private": true` in package.json).
